    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">Cloudblast is the right pick if you specifically want a <strong>10 Gbps + DDoS-included</strong> entry-level KVM VPS in one of three locations and you don't need the global coverage of Vultr or the bare-budget pricing of RackNerd. The €3.6/mo entry is well-priced for what it includes — most competitors at this tier ship 1 Gbps ports and treat DDoS as a paid add-on. Hourly billing makes it a strong fit for short-lived workloads (CI runners, scraping, dev sandboxes).</p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">The trade-offs are the small datacenter footprint, the 1 TB Hong Kong bandwidth cap, and the absence of any public SLA. For pure-budget Linux VPS without the 10 Gbps + DDoS bundle, see our <a href="/vps/racknerd" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd review</a>. For global coverage at €5/mo, see <a href="/vps/vultr" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr</a> or <a href="/vps/linode" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Linode (Akamai)</a>.</p>
